# Crustify artifacts that are regenerable and/or read-only across a wrap/port
# session. Excluded from git tracking so per-agent worktrees stay lean and the
# `git worktree` snapshot only carries the actual mutation surface (`rust/`
# source + build.json + the C edits).
#
# These are NOT hidden from agents: the analysis/codeql trees don't change
# during a wave, so agents read the single shared copy via absolute paths into
# the main checkout (their `analysis_root` / codeql args point there) rather
# than a duplicated per-worktree copy.

# No trailing slashes: these are real directories in the main checkout but
# appear as symlinks inside per-agent worktrees (see worktree.link_shared) -
# a `dir/` pattern would not match the symlink and git would stage it. A bare
# name matches both the directory and the symlink, so neither is ever tracked.
.providers
rust/target
rust.bak
bak
codeql
analysis
targets
tmp
.worktrees
build.json
config.json
crates.json
stats.md
evaluation/